From 4ae3c09c0ebd6e8254b91fb2ebdff8975505d2dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:48:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] video: decode pictures on several threads

The serial decoder cannot keep up with 1080p at 60 pictures a second or
with 4K, so pictures dropped.  Switch to rust_h264's ThreadedDecoder, one
thread for each core up to eight, with the reorder depth the stream
declares so that the first pictures are not held back.  Each picture comes
out in display order with the index of its sample, which gives its time,
so the module that ordered pictures by hand goes.
